<rml>
<head>
	<!-- The chat window and its input (uichat.py ChatWindow, ChatInputSet,
	     ChatLine, ChatModeButton). While the chat flag is on, the Interface
	     makes the facade nui_chat.ChatWindow (controller
	     assets/root/nui_chat.py). CPythonChat keeps the lines; C++ publishes
	     the ones this view shows (feed chat.window.lines), and the lines
	     element builds one element per line, so no Python runs per frame.
	     Closed, the newest five lines show for 5 s above the taskbar on the
	     view shade; open, the history (as tall as history_height, which the
	     sizing bar's drag sets) shows as many lines as it holds above the
	     input row. The body is the 600dp block, placed by the facade with
	     its bottom on the taskbar's top; it takes no pointer but on its
	     interactive parts and never the focus, so a press on a button or a
	     line keeps the field's caret, and the buttons act on mousedown. The
	     input row stays in the layout while the chat is closed, collapsed,
	     so the facade can fill and focus the field in the call that opens
	     the chat. draft is the field's text in a fixture only: the facade
	     keeps it "" and moves the text with set_value, so the binding never
	     changes what the player typed. A press on a link sends nuilink, which the facade turns
	     into the legacy item tooltip, or with left Alt a paste. The closed
	     lines take no pointer but their links, so a press beside a link
	     reaches the world as in legacy; the open history takes it, for the
	     wheel (new: legacy never scrolls the chat window). -->
	<title>chat</title>
	<link type="text/template" href="../../nui.rtpl"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="chat.rcss"/>
</head>
<body template="nui" class="chat nui-below-legacy-ui nui-field-passes-hotkeys nui-field-keeps-focus" data-model="chat">
	<div id="chat" class="chat__block" data-class-is-open="open" data-class-is-quiet="!open &amp;&amp; !view_chat" data-event-nuilink="link(ev.link)">
		<div id="chat-history" class="chat__history">
			<nui-resize id="chat-resize" class="nui-resize--top chat__resize nui-interactive" edge="top" target="chat-history"
				min-height="25" data-attr-height="history_height" data-event-resized="resized(ev.height)"><div class="chat__grip"></div></nui-resize>
			<nui-chat-lines id="chat-lines" class="chat__lines" view="window" step="15"
				data-attr-mode="open ? 'edit' : 'view'" data-event-mousescroll="wheel(ev.wheel_delta_y)"/>
		</div>
		<div id="chat-input-row" class="chat__input-row nui-interactive">
			<button id="chat-mode" class="chat__mode" data-event-mousedown="mode(ev.button)"><span
				data-if="chat_mode == 0">@game.CHAT_NORMAL</span><span
				data-if="chat_mode == 3">@game.CHAT_PARTY</span><span
				data-if="chat_mode == 4">@game.CHAT_GUILD</span><span
				data-if="chat_mode == 6">@game.CHAT_SHOUT</span></button>
			<div id="chat-field" class="chat__field">
				<input id="chat-input" type="text" maxlength="512" class="nui-input chat__input"
					data-attr-value="draft" data-event-change="changed(ev.value, ev.linebreak)"/>
				<span id="chat-mark" class="chat__mark" data-if="mark != ''">{{ mark }}</span>
			</div>
			<span id="chat-send" class="chat__button chat__send nui-has-tooltip" data-event-mousedown="send(ev.button)"><span
				class="nui-tooltip nui-anim chat__tip">@game.CHAT_SEND_CHAT</span></span>
			<span id="chat-whisper" class="chat__button chat__whisper nui-has-tooltip" data-event-mousedown="whisper(ev.button)"><span
				class="nui-tooltip nui-anim chat__tip">@game.CHAT_SEND_MEMO</span></span>
			<span id="chat-log-open" class="chat__button chat__log-open nui-has-tooltip" data-event-mousedown="open_log(ev.button)"><span
				class="nui-tooltip nui-anim chat__tip">@game.CHAT_LOG</span></span>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
